"""
  |OMC_BTS:
  | ------------------------------------------------------------
  |  cell_trace_activate -- Activates Cell Trace on NE
  | ------------------------------------------------------------
  |  Usage: cell_trace_activate -if <IF>, [-vendor, -port <PORT>, -mdt, -lcrid]
  |
  |  -if <IF>
  |         - list of interfaces to be traced. Comma separated list of following values:
  |             s: S1AP interface (eNodeB <-> MME)
  |             x: X2AP interface (eNodeB <-> neighbor eNodeB)
  |             u: Uu interface   (enodeb <-> UE)
  |
  |  -vendor
  |         - flag controls vendor specific tracing. Currently only MAC layer TA (Timing Advance) messages.
  |           By default TA tracing is disabled.
  |
  |  -port <PORT>
  |         - port number of trace collecting entity. The option is needed only in case when default port number
  |           should be overwritten. Default port number is calculated from following formula:
  |
  |           PORT = 40000 + OFFSET + BTS_ID
  |
  |           OFFSET depends on hardware platform:
  |
  |             macro (FSM): 9000
  |             micro (FZM): 7000
  |             pico  (FZP): 8000
  |  -mdt
  |         - changes additional parameters for Cell Trace.
  |
  |  -lcrid
  |         - adds optional parameter 'lcrId' in MTRACE object to specify on which cell activate trace session.
  |
  |  -mid
  |         - activates MTRACE with given id.
"""
